{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Model.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.mkModel\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkModel</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">goal</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Types.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Goal\">Goal</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> (<a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Rat/Basic.html#Rat\">Rat</a>))</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Construct a model that satisfies all constraints in the cutsat model.\nIt also assigns values to integer terms that have not been internalized by the\ncutsat model.\n\nRemark: it uses rational numbers because cutsat may have failed to build an\ninteger model.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Model.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.mkModel","kind":"def","line":72,"name":"Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.mkModel","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Model.lean#L72-L103"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Tactic/Grind/Arith/Cutsat/Model.html#Lean.Meta.Grind.Arith.Cutsat.getAssignment?\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Grind</span>.<span class=\"name\">Arith</span>.<span class=\"name\">Cutsat<